 best  thing that can happen so we can all take  a step back and re-evaluate and reassess  and figure out how we how we avoid this  ever happening again if you ran USA  soccer what would you do would it be the  top priority for you well there are so  many there are so many priorities and  I'll just start by saying I know there's  a lot of heat on um you know Galati  today a lot of heat on Bruce Arena a lot  of heat on on all the people involved  with this sport let's not forget that  none of these things are easy and if  you're on the outside looking in it's  always easy to pick apart what you think  is wrong so I'll preface it with all  that I think the biggest issue in our  country probably is that we have too  many kids that don't play soccer because  they can't afford it or they don't have  the support or they drop out of soccer  because they're burnt out because of  coaches that are overbearing or parents  that are overbearing I think we're  missing out on too many quality players  and you know that's that's the starting  point for all of it what happens when  you're a teenager and then when you're  in you know your late teens and early  20s and professionally that's all  different but the the crux of it for me  would be to start there and work your  way up and figure out how to make that  part better he's landed Donovan former  USA soccer star how are you developed  and developed into maybe the greatest  you know soccer player we've ever had  developed well I was a little bit and  you know Clint Dempsey Tim Howard to  some extent Michael Bradley was the  exception because he  who understood what it was all about so  he got proper coaching and proper  guidance but for all of us we were a  little bit lightning in a bottle and we  sort of just made it on our own but you  can't depend on that right that's not  that's not a recipe for success so I was  developed because I just was a dork at  school who carried a soccer ball around  all day and kicked it against the